            description: "Hardy in Zones 1 and 2. This Canadian apple is represented by bearing trees in Fairbanks. It is productive and moderately precocious in bearing. Fruits are pale green, overlaid with a purplish-red blush, 5 to 6 centimeters diameter. Flesh is crisp and juicy with a good flavor. The fruit is said to keep well and ripens early to mid-September in Fairbanks, mid-September in Southcentral"
        },
        {
