            description: "Hardy in Zone 2. This Canadian apple is one of the leading apples grown in Alaska. A genetic semidwarf resulting from a Melba and Rescue crossing. The tree is very hard and productive. Fruit is 6 to 7 centimeters long, yellow green in color with red blush. Flesh is white with a pleasant tart taste. Makes excellent preserves. Generally, stores longer and considered a better quality fruit than Norland. Ripens late August to September in Southcentral"
